<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Richemont SAfrica no comment on suspension.</title>
<headline>Richemont SAfrica no comment on suspension.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>A South African spokesman for Swiss-based holding firm Richemont AG declined to comment on the suspension of the firm's shares in Switzerland.</p>
<p>&quot;The instructions came directly from Switzerland. Anything I might say would just be speculation,&quot; a spokesman told Reuters.</p>
<p>Earlier Richemont AG shares were suspended in Zurich pending publication of an important announcement in the course of the afternoon, the Swiss stock exchange said.</p>
<p>The Wall Street Journal earlier said Hughes Electric Corp, a unit of General Motors, was in serious talks to invest as much as $1 billion for a 30-percent stake in the Netherlands' NetHold. Holding firm Nethold is half-owned by Richemont and MCL-Multi Choice Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 22 482 1003</p>
